title: Tutorial_Memory_Introduction
---
// Shu Wen: the story opening lives in Assets/Marcus/Scripts/Story/Tutorial/Tutorial.yarn.
// This node starts on the first Memory World visit of a new game.
// Mother's Study dialogue is a separate node below; do not add memory_complete to this opening node.
<<detour Tutorial>>
//You have entered the Memory World. Echoes of the past can help restore what has been lost. #line:tutorial_intro_001
//Move with WASD or the arrow keys. Hold E near the cabinet key to reveal its Echo. #line:tutorial_intro_002
//Release E, then hold E again to capture the Echo. Hold 1 near the locked cabinet to replay it. #line:tutorial_intro_003
//Collect the memory fragments, then open the Manual with R to reconstruct the memory. Your objective will guide you. #line:tutorial_intro_004
===

title: Tutorial_Mother_Message
---
// Starts after restoring and entering the Study. Edit Mother's approved dialogue here.
Mother: Placeholder: Mother's message begins here. #line:tutorial_mother_001
Mother: Placeholder: Add Mother's next line here. #line:tutorial_mother_002
Mother: Placeholder: Add Mother's final line here. #line:tutorial_mother_003
<<memory_complete>>
===

title: Recorder
---

Mum: The memory machine is an asset that is passed down in our family for generations.

<<cameraShift studyFragmentTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Next, collect the fragment near the Study.
Mem: Hold E beside that glowing fragment to collect it.
<<cameraReturn>>

===

title: Recorder_Study_Collected
---
// The Study fragment was collected first. The controller queues the appropriate next step.
Mum: The memory machine is an asset that is passed down in our family for generations.

===

title: FamilyPhoto
---
Jade: It’s a photo of a family. That child… It looks like me when I was young.
 
Jade: Then are those two my parents?
 
===


title: FogLocked
---
Mem: This area has not been reconstructed.

Mem: Find fragments and clues to reconstruct it.

===

title: Tutorial_Cabinet_Locked
---
Mem: You can't touch or change remembered objects in the Memory World. You'll need to capture an Echo first.
Mem: The cabinet is locked. We need the Cabinet Key Echo before we can open it.
<<cameraShift keyEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Look at the glowing key above the fridge. Its Echo remembers an action from the past.
Mem: Hold E near the key to reveal its Echo. Release E, then hold E again to capture it.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Key_Echo_Captured
---
Mem: You captured the Cabinet Key Echo. It is now stored in slot 1.
<<cameraShift cabinetEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Stand beside the locked cabinet and hold 1 to replay the Echo.
Mem: The remembered action will unlock the cabinet.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Cabinet_Opened
---
<<cameraShift cabinetEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: The cabinet is open. A recorder fragment was hidden inside.
Mem: Echoes are actions remembered by this world. Replaying the Key Echo repeated the action of unlocking the cabinet.
Mem: Hold E beside the recorder to collect its memory fragment.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Reconstruction_Ready
---
Mem: You have collected all three memory fragments. It is time to reconstruct the memory.
Mem: Open the Manual with R and select Reconstruction.
Mem: Drag the words into the blanks, then choose Reconstruct. The memory will reveal the Study.
===

title: Tutorial_Find_Mother_Fragment
---
<<cameraShift photoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: One fragment remains: the family photo.
Mem: Hold E beside it to collect the Mother fragment. Then we can reconstruct the memory.
<<cameraReturn>>
===
